    "observations": [
     {
      "index": 0,
      "verdict": "accepted",
      "reason": "booking-tool.py:106-117 defines overlaps() using datetime.strptime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M') and returns True only when start1 < end2 and start2 < end1; equal endpoints fail, so directly touching intervals are not overlapping. The observation matches the source."
     },
     {
      "index": 1,
      "verdict": "accepted",
      "reason": "booking-tool.py:377-382 loops every stored booking, runs p.search(booking['description']) at line 378, and returns HTTP 400 at line 382 when the parsed lab name equals the request lab and overlaps(...) is true. Accurate."
     },
     {
      "index": 2,
      "verdict": "accepted",
      "reason": "booking-tool.py:271-326 gates delete() on an authenticated session (273-279), validates id/start/end/description (281-291), permits admins while checking ownership for others (274-275, 313-316), extracts previous_user from the stored description (312-316), and rewrites new_data to the JSON file (319-321). Accurate."
     },
     {
      "index": 3,
      "verdict": "accepted",
      "reason": "templates/index.html:45-60 contains the fullCalendar init: header right includes month,agendaWeek,agendaDay (46-50), defaultView is 'month' (51), editable is true (56), and events is '/bookings' (57). Accurate."
     },
     {
      "index": 4,
      "verdict": "accepted",
      "reason": "README.md:51-53 says the tool is a test tool not intended for serious use without evaluation/modification, calls file read/write instead of a database a big disadvantage, and says it may not suit real use cases. Accurate."
     },
     {
      "index": 5,
      "verdict": "accepted",
      "reason": "README.md:5-17 documents RESOURCE_INFO (names and colors), DB_FILE, USER_DB, LOG_FILE, ADMIN_INFO, HOST, PORT, TZ, REGISTRATION_ALLOWED, ALLOWED_DOMAINS, TITLE, FOOTER_MESSAGE, and RESOURCE_NAME. Accurate."
     }
    ],
    "issues": [
     "acceptance/probe.py:156-172 (A02) never verifies that the rejected zero-length claim added no row. After the 400 response it calls only touching() (lines 91-92), whose strict overlap test cannot see a 14:00-14:00 ghost against 14:00-16:00, and the later exactly-once check counts only the new id. A server that returns 400 but also inserts the zero-length row still passes, contrary to AUTHOR_INPUT.json:13 ('adds nothing') and the A02 goal 'creates no block'.",
     "acceptance/probe.py:157 requires the zero-length rejection to be exactly INVALID_INTERVAL, but VIEW_ARCH.md:86 lists both INVALID_INTERVAL and INVALID_DURATION and VIEW_ARCH.md:92 only states a duration of 30-240 minutes. A spec-following implementation can reasonably return 400 INVALID_DURATION, while AUTHOR_INPUT.json:13 requires only 400; the probe is stricter than the pinned contract.",
     "acceptance/probe.py:185-188 checks only that error.conflicts contains the original id and that error.message contains that id. It never verifies conflicting start/end values. VIEW_ARCH.md:88 requires error.conflicts objects with id/start/end and a message naming both intervals, and AUTHOR_INPUT.json:14 requires naming the 14:00-16:00 reservation and its times; an implementation returning only the id passes A03.",
     "acceptance/README.md:21,40 and VIEW_ARCH.md:114 claim the probe checks both fixed windows before writing and exits 2 with status not_run when setup is unsafe. The probe instead checks 09:00-10:00 inside A01 and creates it (probe.py:134-135), then checks 14:00-16:00 only later in A02 (probe.py:158-160). If 14:00 is occupied, the 09:00 probe claim may already have been written, and occupied windows become failed cases with exit 1, not not_run; exit 2 is used only for the initial GET failure (probe.py:101-107)."
    ],
    "summary": "The leaf scope, source citations, and design distinction are sound, and the Thursday claim/conflict/cancel journey is covered end to end. The acceptance layer has blocking contract gaps: A02 does not verify that the zero-length refusal leaves no row, A02 hardcodes an error code the architecture does not pin, A03 does not verify the conflict times required by the API, and the documented not_run/refuse-to-proceed safety behavior is not implemented because the probe can write the 09:00 claim before discovering that 14:00 is occupied."
   },
